~ matt_ch2_quest3_start
Matt: We elders never catch too much, leaving time for the sea to recover. This is respect for nature.[#hint=Collect traditional sea protection concepts]
- How do you decide when the sea needs to rest?
	do DialogueChoices.record_choice("matt_ch2_quest3_start", "timing", "curious")
	Matt: We learn that from many years of experience. You are both for the good of the sea! Traditional experience and new methods can be used together! Learning from each other can make things better.
- Resting the sea is also protecting people's future life.
	do DialogueChoices.record_choice("matt_ch2_quest3_start", "future", "empathetic")
	Matt: You get it, boy. You are both for the good of the sea! Traditional experience and new methods can be used together! Learning from each other can make things better.
- Maybe Matt's old wisdom and Kai's new ideas can work side-by-side.
	do DialogueChoices.record_choice("matt_ch2_quest3_start", "combine", "action")
	Matt: That is a thoughtful opinion. You are both for the good of the sea! Traditional experience and new methods can be used together! Learning from each other can make things better.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_quest3_matt_done()
