# ===== Chapter 2 optional coastal exploration =====

~ fishing_boat_start
Fishing boat: This small boat uses a narrow net and carries only what the village needs.
- Why does the boat use a narrow net?
	Fishing boat: It helps the crew avoid sweeping up young fish and damaging the seabed.
- Taking only what is needed leaves more for tomorrow.
	Fishing boat: Sustainable fishing keeps both the village and the ocean healthy.
- I will remember to respect the sea's limits.
	Fishing boat: Every careful choice helps the next generation of fishers.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_fishing_boat_inspected()
=> END

~ rockside_sign_start
Rockside warning sign: Slippery rocks and fast tides ahead. Observe from a safe distance and never leave rubbish behind.
- Why can the rocks become dangerous so quickly?
	Rockside warning sign: A rising tide can cover the safe path within minutes.
- Wildlife lives between these rocks too.
	Rockside warning sign: Walk carefully and leave shells, crabs and tide pools undisturbed.
- I will check the tide and keep the coast clean.
	Rockside warning sign: Safe visitors can protect both themselves and the shoreline.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_rockside_sign_read()
=> END

~ tide_observation_complete
Player: Low tide reveals the shore, rising water brings feeding fish, high tide covers the rocks, and the falling tide carries life back toward the sea.
Matt: Well observed. Reading the tide helps us fish safely while giving coastal habitats time to recover.
=> END

~ advaita_ch3_start
Advaita: We make traditional pastries and hold thanksgiving ceremonies during the harvest festival. Thank the earth for the harvest, and thank the people around us.
Player: Sounds so meaningful! Can I learn it?
Advaita: Of course!
do QuestState.mark_chapter3_quest1_advaita_done()
=> END

